=4 Walkthrough
* To begin this quest you must have traded an {i:Unlit Lantern|Unlit Lantern|1138} to the Altar of Rancor and received the {i:Rancor Flame|Rancor Flame|1139} at some point before. It helps to have a Rancor Flame on you.
* Once you have used a {i:Rancor Flame|Rancor Flame|1139}, talk to {n:Jakoh Wahcondalo} in {z:Kazham} who will tell you to leave her village. The other NPCs in the room tell you to go the {z:Den of Rancor}/{z:Temple of Uggalepih} complex to be cleansed and then come back.
** You get the title "Excommunicate of Kazham" as soon as this quest becomes active.
* You will need to obtain at least 1 {i:Unlit Lantern|Unlit Lantern|1138} to cleanse the Rancor.
** The lanterns are dropped by {m:Tonberry Maledictors|Tonberry Maledictor}.
** Ideally, it is easiest to use 4 players with 4 lanterns, however you just need to light all 4 lamps at the Altar. You can actually solo this by making 4 trips back and forth between the {i:Rancor Flame|Rancor Flame|1139} and the altar. The altar seems to stay lit for quite a while.
* Once you have the {i:Unlit Lanterns|Unlit Lantern|1138}, go back to the main entrance and make all right turns to exit at F-5. Now hug the left wall to re-enter the temple at H-11.
* Once in the temple, head to I-10 and defeat the {m:Temple Guardian} to open the door.
* Past the guardian's door, head north to I-7 inside the paintings room. A {k:Paintbrush of souls} is needed to proceed into the {z:Den of Rancor}.
* Once you are in the Den of Rancor, go to the Altar of Rancor at D/E-5. You can easily get there by hugging the right wall from where you enter the Den. Once there, the {i:Unlit Lanterns|Unlit Lantern|1138} must be traded to the Altar of Rancor to receive a {i:Rancor Flame|Rancor Flame|1139}.
* Once you have your Rancor Flames, you want to visit the other Altar of Rancor at I/J-13. Trade the {i:Rancor Flames|Rancor Flame|1139} to the Altar of Rancor.
* After the fourth lantern is lit, a bomb NM called {m:Rancor Torch} will appear.
* Kill the {m:Rancor Torch} and head back to {z:Kazham} and talk to the Chieftainess for your reward.

